---
export const title = 'Keyboard and accessibility';
export const order = 300;
---

<p>
  The popup is a <strong>non-modal</strong> dialog (<code>role="dialog"</code>), named by the step's
  headline and described by its body. The scrim is only drawn: it takes no clicks, so the page stays
  usable and the person can try the highlighted control while the step explains it. A modal tour would
  make the page inert, including the target, and trap people who want to look around.
</p>
<p>
  Focus moves into the popup at each step, so a screen reader reads the new headline, and returns to where
  it was when the tour ends. Escape ends the tour. While focus is in the popup, Left and Right (mirrored in
  right-to-left layouts) go back and forward. The target scrolls into view smoothly, or instantly when the
  person prefers reduced motion; the spotlight then does not animate between steps either. In forced-colors
  mode the spotlight is drawn as a Highlight outline.
</p>
<p>
  The strings are translated with <code>setPeacockStrings()</code>: <code>tourBack</code>,
  <code>tourNext</code>, <code>tourDone</code>, <code>tourSkip</code> and the shared
  <code>stepPosition</code> ("Step 2 of 4").
</p>
